  "label": "general internet audience",
  "description": "The meme is designed for a broad, general internet audience familiar with consumer culture and online humor tropes. It leverages relatable experiences such as receiving a free item with missing parts, which is a common source of frustration and humor across demographics. The visual of a domestic kitchen scene with two people is universally accessible, and the text overlay ('free dishwasher', 'missing parts') is a straightforward, widely understood internet meme format. The humor is situational and benign, targeting anyone who has experienced consumer disappointment or irony in promotional offers, without targeting any specific protected group or community.",
